# Code owners — required reviewers per path.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# `docs/decisions/000-ci-security-gates.md` ends by naming the one thing none of
# the CI gates cover: a merge to `main` that changes the workflows themselves.
# Once a modified `ci.yml` is the definition on `main`, every gate runs exactly
# as that file now says, and any attestation it produces is genuinely valid.
#
# This file plus branch protection's **"Require review from Code Owners"** is the
# closest thing the repo has to a lever on that. It is still not a control on its
# own — an owner reviewing their own change is no review — but it removes the
# case where a `.github/` change merges with nobody having looked.
#
# SHIPPED INERT ON PURPOSE
#
# Every rule below is commented out. A CODEOWNERS entry naming a user or team
# that cannot be resolved is **silently ignored by GitHub** — the file stays in
# place, the branch-protection box stays ticked, and nothing is ever required.
# That is the exact failure `docs/decisions/001-writing-a-guard.md` is about: a
# guard that reads as safety while checking nothing. An obviously-empty file is
# honest; a plausible-looking broken one is not.
#
